  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "A strange light dims into a tall man on a Southern Border battlefield where Liu Hao has disappeared. The narration names him Jun Shen Guang, a rank eight light path Gu Immortal and supreme elder of one of the ten great ancient sects, recently recruited into Heavenly Court by Fairy Zi Wei. He specializes in tracking and is kept as backup in case Southern Border immortals wound Fang Yuan and leave him open to pursuit.",
      "chapters": [
        1604
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_southern_border",
        "char_liu_hao",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "char_fairy_zi_wei",
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He is a tall man. He has a pair of thin white brows that extend toward the outer sides of his face. The eyes under those snowy brows are closed. He wears white clothes unstained by dust. His robe, skin, and hair all release a faint radiance.",
      "chapters": [
        1604
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "With his eyes closed he still tracks the outside world clearly. He confirms Liu Hao vanished at the site, inspects dao mark traces of a pure time path immortal formation that hid from Xia Cha and Lu Wei Yin, finds no further clues, and leaves as a Southern Border Immortal Gu House approaches so he will not be mistaken for an enemy.",
      "chapters": [
        1604
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_xia_cha",
        "char_lu_wei_yin",
        "sys_immortal_gu_house"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Heavenly Court later uses his list of loyal Gu Immortal seeds when choosing mortals for costly nurturing after the immortal graveyard is destroyed.",
      "chapters": [
        1970
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "gu-immortal-seeds",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
